From bb087049844ca7a8d90ca1f6683731012fce65f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 10:04:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Mobile Organic visual refresh (OrbitPane Mobile design)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements the OrbitPane Mobile.dc.html Claude Design handoff (direction
1a): a mobile-scoped visual reskin onto the Organic design system —
warm-ink dark ground, terracotta accent, sage success, Caprasimo/Figtree/
IBM Plex Mono type, 16/24/28/999 radii — layered on top of the existing
CSS custom-property theme so desktop is untouched (everything is gated
behind @media (max-width: 768px)).

- index.css: mobile Organic token overrides for dark + light theme;
  index.html: loads the three fonts.
- Retint the handful of hardcoded (non-token) colors used on mobile
  screens: execution timeline step categories, login accent orb, avatar
  gradients, provider badges/dots, mission-control accent rule.
- Add TaskCapsule: the persistent "N running / N queued / context %"
  pill between the header and message list (the collapsed top-pill form
  of the task pod), opening the existing full-screen WorkspaceInspector.
- Add PreferencesSheet: a real 主题/选择运行模型/通知与反馈 settings
  surface as a bottom sheet (consistent with the app's existing sheet
  idiom), wired to the real theme, model, notification-permission, and a
  new persisted haptics-enabled flag (nativeFeedback.ts).
- Convert CommandPalette (⌘K) into a mobile bottom sheet.
- Fix theme-color meta + Toast icon tint for the mobile palette.

Verified: tsc --noEmit, vite build, oxlint all clean; Login (dark/light)
and Welcome/Mission Control screens visually spot-checked against the
design at 390x844.

Not in scope (called out in the handoff as out of scope or unmocked):
1b (light-paper) and 1c (terracotta cap-header) variants were not
requested; PwaInstallPrompt colors are untouched (not one of the named
design screens).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
